A||||3||Zoom88||Rear Decklid, does it fit ?||||1||
Z||000000||Zoom88||12-14-2001||08:07 AM|||| Can I use a rear decklid without the hump on my 88 Formula, ( Want to use it with one of those rear mustang scoops ) Don't want to cut my original since I need to buy another, will it work ?<P> <FONT COLOR="red">MERRY</FONT><FONT COLOR="green">CHRISTMAS</FONT> Everyone !!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-14-2001||08:58 AM||||If you mean an 84 that has the grate on it, yes you can use it. If you mean the flat one from a fastback GT, no you can't. You can only use notchback decklids on a notchback and fastback decklids on a fastback. All notchback decklids except 84 have the hump.<BR>The fastback decklids are raised to meet the body and slightly longer due to the taillight differences.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||12-14-2001||08:59 AM||||The hump was added in 1985 to allow the V6 to clear the decklid, but since you're going to cut the 84 decklid for the scoop, you may not have any problems with clearance if you cut out the right areas.<P>Not much of an answer, is it ? Kinda one of those "try it and let the rest of us know" scenarios...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zoom88||12-14-2001||08:26 PM||||Thanks , I guess I really need to see one of the 84. Actually learned something from you two, thanks. Didn't know about the 84 , the grate etc;||||reg||1
